   $q$Read the sentences: (A) Rinse all the soap out with warm water. (B) Wet the dog's fur with warm water. (C) Dry the dog with a large, soft towel. (D) Rub dog shampoo into the wet fur. Which is the most logical order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-time-order"},{"text":"B, D, C, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-time-order"},{"text":"D, B, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-time-order"},{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, D, A, C$q$, $q$The fur must be wet before the shampoo goes on, the soap must be rinsed out after it is added, and drying comes last. Order B, D, C, A is wrong because it dries the dog before rinsing out the soap.$q$, 'draft', null)
