  ('ee3f566c-29d3-5d24-980c-4eb41595225a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Read: "(1) Every spring, our town holds a kite festival in Harbor Park. (2) Families build kites shaped like dragons, fish, and stars. (3) Judges give ribbons for the highest, the most colorful, and the funniest kites. (4) My cousin lives in a town near the mountains. (5) When the festival ends, everyone helps pick up string and paper from the grass." Which sentence does not belong?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 4","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 5","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-concluding-sentence"},{"text":"Sentence 3","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 2","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 4$q$, $q$The paragraph is about the kite festival, and where the cousin lives has nothing to do with it. Sentence 5 belongs because it tells how the festival ends.$q$, 'draft', null)
