  ('a606ec44-a8fa-5481-9c8a-3ff10e775fa0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The first paragraph of an essay explains the benefits of a school recycling club. The second paragraph explains problems the club has faced. Which sentence best begins the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"For example, the club made colorful posters for the hallway.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-for-contrast"},{"text":"Despite these benefits, the club has also faced some challenges.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In addition, the club collects paper and cans every Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"addition-for-contrast"},{"text":"As a result, more students joined the club this year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"cause-for-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Despite these benefits, the club has also faced some challenges.$q$, $q$"Despite these benefits" points back to paragraph 1, and "challenges" introduces the problems in paragraph 2, so this sentence links the two. "In addition" is wrong because it adds another positive detail instead of turning to the problems.$q$, 'draft', null)
