  ('723813d5-4ee4-5760-be2f-f7e921654d5e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentences: (A) After that, they tested the water at each spot every week for a month. (B) To begin, the students picked three spots along Willow Creek. (C) Finally, they shared their results with the town council. (D) When the month was over, they made a chart comparing the three spots. Which is the most logical order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-time-order"},{"text":"A, B, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-time-order"},{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":true},{"text":"B, A, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-too-early"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, A, D, C$q$, $q$"To begin" starts the project, "After that" follows the first step, "When the month was over" comes after a month of testing, and "Finally" ends it. Order B, D, A, C is wrong because the chart is made "when the month was over," which must come after the month of testing in A.$q$, 'draft', null)
