   $q$Read: "Hummingbirds beat their wings many times every second. Flying this way uses a great deal of energy. They must eat often." Which revision of the last sentence best shows how it connects to the sentences before it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Before that, they must eat often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-order"},{"text":"For instance, they must eat often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-for-effect"},{"text":"For this reason, they must eat often.","is_correct":true},{"text":"However, they must eat often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-for-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For this reason, they must eat often.$q$, $q$The second sentence says flying uses a great deal of energy, and needing to eat often is the result of that, so "For this reason" shows the cause and effect. "However" is wrong because eating often fits with using lots of energy instead of going against it.$q$, 'draft', null)
